# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_resolve_js_mock_dir.py" "JS-MOCK-DIR GATE: PASS" "js mock dir precision" "JS/TS bare-import precision: a bare single-segment import names an external package, so it must not resolve to a Jest/Vitest test-double file under __mocks__/__mock__/__fixtures__ (the mock shadows the external package and is never a production import target); drops those candidates for a bare web import while keeping relative/aliased/multi-segment imports and real non-mock local modules" "JS/TS false src->test coupling: import Vue from 'vue' / import \$ from 'jquery' matched spec/frontend/__mocks__/<pkg>/index.js decoys; measured 1388 such edges on gitlabhq (37 surviving hub-dampening as real false couplings); the fix mirrors the Rust/CSharp/Go separate-test-target exclusion and is recall-safe (a real local module under __mocks__ is never imported by a bare name)" 14
